  {
   "id": "SyYIh2_bAwAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2024-07-10T14:55:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: Multilevel 2PL with discrimination parameters at the cluster level.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Sebastian,<div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t believe this is possible to do in the current implementation of mixedmirt() as the slopes are assumed to be equal across the person/clusters (if they are unequal, this gets into DIF territory). I haven&#39;t read that paper though, so perhaps this is something different. Note that for these types of random effects models it&#39;s nearly always better to use dedicated MCMC estimators as they become unstable and high-dimensional quite quickly (e.g., see brms or stan for implementation). HTH.</div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Oct 5, 2023 at 7:01 PM &#39;Sebastian Castro-Alvarez&#39; via mirt-package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
